# Docker reads .dockerignore from the BUILD CONTEXT root. docker-compose.yml
# builds with context: ./server, so the repository-root .dockerignore never
# applied here — `COPY . .` copied the host's 139 MB node_modules into the image,
# overwriting the modules installed inside it. That is why the container died on
# startup with "GLIBC_2.38 not found": the host's sqlite3 native binary (built for
# a newer glibc) replaced the one built for node:20-slim.
**/node_modules
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
coverage
.sqlite-data
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.log
